# Chat title — workspace folder prefix

When renaming a chat thread (user asks to rename, or you call `rename_chat`),
**always put the current workspace folder name first** in brackets:

```text
[<workspace-folder>] <short title>
```

## How to derive the prefix

- Use the **basename of the Cursor workspace / project root** (the folder
  opened as the project), not the git remote org and not a random topic tag.
- Examples:
  - Workspace `/Users/…/sume/sume-com` → `[sume-com] …`
  - Workspace `/Users/…/other-app` → `[other-app] …`
- Keep the bracket token stable for that workspace. Do not invent alternate
  spellings (`[sume]`, `[SumeCom]`, etc.) when the folder is `sume-com`.

## Rules

- Prefix is **required** on every rename; never drop it when the topic changes.
- Put the folder token **first**; then a short human title.
- Do not rename proactively — only when the user asks (or product policy
  already requires a rename). When you do rename, still apply this prefix.
- If the title already starts with the correct `[folder]`, keep it and only
  update the part after the prefix.

## Examples

- `[sume-com] Org pooled wallet BP`
- `[sume-com] Railway avatar lookup`
- `[docs-site] Nav collapse`
